# async-cancel-safety

Ensure futures used in
tokio::select! branches are cancellation-safe

## Why It Matters
...
polls multiple futures concurrently and, the moment one branch completes, it drops every other branch — including any state those futures held. A future that was halfway through reading bytes into a local buffer, or halfway through draining a channel into a Vec, loses that progress silently. This is not a compiler error; it compiles fine and the bug only surfaces under concurrent load. Tokio documents which of its primitives are cancellation-safe; everything else must be treated with care.

